## What the report says

It's a version-based scan of Apache httpd (ports 80/443) on `136.68.140.144`. It flags ~60 CVEs and asks us to either restrict access or upgrade to 2.4.69.

I can't confirm these CVE IDs or the 2.4.69 release from my side, so verify the latest version at httpd.apache.org before acting.

## What needs diagnosing first

I won't guess the cause yet. The scanner may be matching a banner rather than the real package, and many of these CVEs only apply if specific modules or configs are active:

| Group | Applies only if |
|---|---|
| Windows-only (CVE-2026-59685, 2024-38472, 2025-59775) | Host is Windows. Not applicable on Ubuntu. |
| mod_proxy_ftp, mod_dav/dav_fs/dav_lock, mod_ldap, mod_md, mod_proxy_ajp, mod_userdir, mod_vhost_alias, mod_auth_digest | That module is loaded and configured. |
| Core/mod_rewrite/mod_proxy (2024-38xxx) | Version <2.4.60, or an unsafe RewriteRule. |

Ubuntu also backports security fixes without bumping the upstream version, so the banner can look vulnerable when the package is already patched.

